  "worked_solution": "First, from the diagram, notice that $∠BCA$ and $∠BCD$ are supplementary. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠BCA+m∠BCD & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BCA+y & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠BCA & ={180}^{∘}-y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $△ABC$ is an isosceles triangle where $\\overset{―}{AC}≅\\overset{―}{BC}$, the base angles must be equal:\n\n$$\nm∠B=m∠A={56}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the interior angles of any triangle sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠A+m∠B+m∠BCA & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {56}^{∘}+{56}^{∘}+({180}^{∘}-y) & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ y & ={112}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
